  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_7c7e3c2acd304ad3b717fec4288c7e12",
      "statement": "`sincpro_framework/introspection/` is the single module that knows the bus's internal shape: it reads `feature_bus.feature_registry`, `app_service_bus.app_service_registry` and `dto_registry`, and consumers such as the entrypoint catalog build on it rather than reaching into `FrameworkBus` themselves.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/catalog.py#L134-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83db79e3c3fb8b7202353d9c106753d378f5a52f082dead5c8785341228c7981:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/catalog.py#L14-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:69c52793e97c7ed959433fd34e1a00179fd1c4d79cd0dc8f2f66682af6addee2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/__init__.py#L1-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c41ae1b27783d630aa7e8178fe9c51f39e1be41ed5b4cdfc1993a0d6cab7feb0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L1-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:35bda086827e55f1bbc582eb91909e942da7cebda79af35e74104ae2708758a3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_743a2282d6c24a4b86ac23b66b1703e3",
      "statement": "`built_bus()` guards every reader: when `was_initialized` is false or `bus` is `None` it raises `ValueError` with the `NOT_BUILT` message (\"Framework must be built before introspection\"), and it never builds the framework itself — unlike `Catalog`, whose constructor calls `build_root_bus()` on an unbuilt instance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/catalog.py#L47-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5d2625e90df60b2d01b5478cb93efa9a34372082a5de4014df26bc2bd6348d2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L21-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d0e606cb4e197b9716e8a3ee7852dab0bf62c51834037d7c5ea0095edfca9552:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L72-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c0ed042aaf7565c3e34c7d8fd299364fbe38ed5bc622b71555f213510f2854f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/use_bus.py#L87-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44108ac22c748ae030097a7ee603037f7627f33402b4391d50ed9242010854d7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_introspection.py#L76-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d43fde86666b9f9fdefd5ed15cf26f275d3cc33ecf5fc02854b1e61eb0f43a66:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5056087ef2234a40949917737657f6e7",
      "statement": "The `bus is None` half of the `built_bus()` guard is load-bearing because `build_root_bus()` flips `was_initialized = True` before the facade is materialised, so a build that raises leaves the instance claiming to be initialized with `bus` still `None`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L72-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c0ed042aaf7565c3e34c7d8fd299364fbe38ed5bc622b71555f213510f2854f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/use_bus.py#L123-L130",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47a271010e453e66033cd0f4055110035ee9a4621399dbe5f617cc541f76f19f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3069fd84c30b4fb2aec4a26e63656f90",
      "statement": "`dto_registry` is a build-time snapshot: `build_root_bus()` resolves the container provider once and assigns the resolved `{name: DTO class}` dict onto the facade, which is the copy all three introspection readers consume (`features()`, `app_services()` look names up in it; `dtos()` enumerates it), so a rebuild refreshes what introspection sees.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L98-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bfbd8511d1285ea5e1255c52cbe33c7c1324f5671b75aec2685cc960093e4f1c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/ioc.py#L119-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea8c7e7cbdeb7a60b83811aa9b1abcef5178e1e101920a4a47b4b9e0b0a6a4de:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/ioc.py#L45-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42f57137a47cee839ca965addb87083b3c5305a8ef8be823255420155e1c43aa:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/use_bus.py#L128-L128",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e90da8a548eb1d5dedf0ee34be840ad61c57d5232cd56829121fbe9d8e8b774:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/use_bus.py#L142-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c2e132f472fc44e5b0f662c3385586d223980453de7ee8bc6c7c396e41914b89:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_36be3676c6b142a5a80ffd447cd16d2f",
      "statement": "A handler's description is resolved in a fixed four-step order — its own class docstring, then its own `execute` docstring, then the input DTO's own docstring, then the DTO name — where \"own\" means a `cls.__dict__` lookup, so docstrings inherited from `Feature` or `ApplicationService` bases never become the description.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L44-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fffe0f46efb7cde6956b09989a9ac76b7bacaa0b6b89019b71b3b00f0d081e4d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/sincpro_abstractions.py#L141-L153",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dee1cf037808ddc6ceccb383a6a915d3fc4fff088da96896818b8991fccab601:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_introspection.py#L51-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67c74d852744efc03f85b2f2c40cd1426cb90371f5372e96e5d1833e047f035a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2630d4e1c5dc4631b16cd34cc137f5b5",
      "statement": "`FeatureOrAppServiceMetadata` describes one registered handler with exactly `name`, `type`, the live `instance`, the input `dto` class and a non-nullable `description`; `DtoMetadata` describes one DTO with `name`, `type` and a nullable `description`. Both are `DataTransferObject` subclasses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L115-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b738b035508e0967de932ca0da507f232305f34ade2fafc6cb9dc1499b1dab83:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L23-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a3f564924d2671c6803a7cfb9e711467448256f2a897ebb1bd75c369b0560012:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L88-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0dae7dd4b8acfe56c9d040392106fc46f7b45f3bbcf38e89aedfecdfe9ef1b3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e0add87c0f394af1b412ed459bfee749",
      "statement": "`dtos()` uses its own rule rather than the handler ladder: it carries the DTO's own docstring only, with no fallback, so an undocumented DTO's `description` is `None`, whereas a handler's description is always a string because the ladder ends at the DTO name.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L112-L118",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:22b513ec9c4651f9fe2a2a09aeb50e3c29979523d1d22d38ff373ae8b06c45cc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L64-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:813c7a418b794faa68f05a2356d75bb966280ab0336218fbf73afe2805ee8210:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_introspection.py#L67-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c8ebb105232468355739fef860a8194b3957d36d07daef4ca0439864be2c836d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_360afd489611474a9bc893ed02c3c0ee",
      "statement": "A name present in a layer registry but absent from `dto_registry` is silently skipped (`continue`, no warning and no partial entry) by `_describe_all`, which is exactly the state left by `FeatureBus.register_feature` / `ApplicationServiceBus.register_app_service`: those methods mutate the materialised `{name: instance}` dict without touching the container or `dto_registry`, making such a handler invisible to `features()`/`app_services()` and to every host built on them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L30-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d8c070c09a507301517ac83bf4d2eb886097377c05d96e0a8f1195975760cc95:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L82-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5290a5ae4a1b9abb6230541aaad19764a9029edd985c1ca48dbe6dc1a480f0e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/entrypoints/catalog.py#L134-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83db79e3c3fb8b7202353d9c106753d378f5a52f082dead5c8785341228c7981:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L78-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:13494601054d7aa6981fb7bf57bdd9c29fd54d1d868f4178424ab8cbf6dc5e7b:"
        },
        {
